      <activity id="e03bcc09-b981-5202-8d5c-f05e16e710fa" activityNameId="f0bc1ca2-e9fe-5fa5-a0af-81095b494e47" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, at service station</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, at service station
The inventory for "ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, at service station, CH" is modelled with data of the regional distribution of petrol in Switzerland.;
CAS number: 000064-17-5; 
Formula: C2H6O ; 
Synonyms: Alkohol, alcohol dehydrated, algrain, Anhydrol, cologne spirit, cologne spirits (alcohol), Denatured alcohol, Ethyl alcohol, Ethanol, ethanol 200 proof, Ethanol absolute, ethyl hydrate, ethyl hydroxide, fermentation alcohol, grain alcohol; 
UUID: e37e233d-4a62-33af-83d3-a1e281eeb7d7
Supply of ethanol at service stations in Swtzerland including ethanol production and transports.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Switzerland with standard transport distances and standard distribution.
Technology: Production of ethanol from biomass.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: World ethanol production was around 276 Mio hl in 2003.
Sampling: Literature data. 
Extrapolations: Transports are modelled with standard distances.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e37e233d-4a62-33af-83d3-a1e281eeb7d7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
